New checks the existing client_faults.py / client_contract.py do not cover:
R1 prompt wakeup on instantly detectable faults, R2 resources after 300
crash/replace cycles and instant close(), R3 pending table after failure,
R4 late answer / SIGSTOP, R5 lone surrogate -> EngineError without pending
leak, R6 use after close / close during calls, R7 missing binary on
replacement -> EngineError, R8 text-unparseable snapshot (id:null reply) must
not restart the shared process, R9 no killpg on an already reaped pid.

On baseline d69bbaf: R1-R4 pass, R5-R9 fail (see audit log
bin_client_robustness_BEFORE_FIX). Hooked into verify.sh and verify-prebuilt.sh.

(cherry picked from commit 1df3ef8de84a143491d2249723d83c0b1d144ba2)

